# Sulcus: the ice planet's first circuit on its own blocks (docs/blocks-ice.md), driven with the
# ski car. Version 2: it climbs and drops. The start stands on a mesa 24 m up, where the car is
# slow: a tight right at once, then a long progressive left that drops two levels down a cutting,
# speed building into the slide. At the bottom, fast ice: a banked progressive sweeper and a long
# S at full speed, then a banked progressive left that climbs back up a level, slowing the car
# for the snow. The snow winds over a plateau, slow: a banked right, a climb onto the top, a
# long banked left, one snake, a progressive left dropping off the top, a chicane, a hairpin and
# a banked left dropping to the plain. Back on the ice for an S to the finish.
name Sulcus
planet ice
seed 2207
version 2
start 0 0 3 0
# Up on the mesa, slow: a tight right, then down a cutting into the first slide.
turn1_right
curve3_left_down2
slope2_down1
# Fast ice in the valley.
curveberm3_left
sbend4_right
# A banked climb, slowing the car for the snow.
curveberm3_left_up1
checkpoint
# Snow over the plateau: 16 m, slow, every turn different.
to_dirt snow
berm2_right snow
slope2_up1 snow
curveberm2_left snow
snake2 snow
curve2_left_down1 snow
sbend2_right snow
turn1_right snow
curveberm2_left_down1 snow
checkpoint snow
to_road snow
# Ice to the finish.
sbend3_left
straight
finish

terrain hills 8.0
terrain relief 12.0
# The start mesa, 24 m, stretched down the drop so the road runs down a cutting into it.
landform mesa -30 70 40 24 120 -38
# The plateau the snow winds over, 16 m.
landform mesa 300 40 60 16 160 0
# Rock framing the circuit: a butte inside the ice loop, walls to the north and the south,
# buttes to the east.
landform butte 70 140 16 18
landform mesa 120 440 60 40 260 90
landform mesa 120 -330 50 30 260 90
landform butte -210 110 28 26
landform butte -180 -120 22 20
